                [
                    138.0,
                    1328.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "We also assume the existence of public and private information. Public information includes disclosed firm fundamentals and debt structure. In addition, some traders are able to observe private firms' signals about near-term liquidity needs. In either case, following Easley et al. (1996a), we assume that the trading volume aggregates all public and private information.",
